---
// src/pages/bucknell/index.astro  →  arizvi.com/bucknell
// Hub for the Bucknell business analytics search: how I teach, the courses, and classes to try.
// Each course has its own page. Not linked from the nav; sends noindex.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import CurriculumMap from '../../components/CurriculumMap.astro';
import { arrows, courses, catalogue, students } from '../../data/bucknell';

const principles = [
  ['Build the course backwards from the outcome.', 'Each course ends in work a manager could use, and every week builds toward it.'],
  ['Personalize within a defined structure.', 'Everyone learns the same methods. Each student picks the decision or dataset they apply them to.'],
  ['Learn on real problems.', 'Real clients and real constraints wherever I can get them.'],
  ['Test the teaching itself.', 'Mid-term feedback in every course, with changes made before the term ends. In MSCI 543 it moved the exams to paper.'],
];
---
<Base title="Bucknell" description="The courses Ali Rizvi would teach in Bucknell's Analytics & Operations Management department, and how he teaches them." noindex>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="intro-grid">
      <div class="text">
        <p class="label">Bucknell · Analytics &amp; Operations Management</p>
        <h1>Teaching analytics at Bucknell</h1>
        <p class="tagline">I teach analytics the way I used it in industry: {arrows('decision -> model -> recommendation.', true)}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="photo"><img src="/media/headshot.jpg" alt="Ali Rizvi" width="400" height="500" /></div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <Section label="How I teach" id="approach">
    <ol class="principles">
      {principles.map(([head, line]) => <li><strong>{head}</strong> {line}</li>)}
    </ol>
    <p class="muted principles-note">9 course runs at Waterloo between 2021 and 2024, ~700 students, classes of 40 to 180. The classes on the course pages are small invented businesses, so the numbers can be checked. Each course also has a full pack: the syllabus, every week, every lab with what passes, the rubrics and a sample exam, written the way I run a course. The stories beside them are from the work: Alexa at Amazon, the A/B tests I ran inside an e-commerce retailer, compliance models at Morgan Stanley, and a clinical trial I sit close to at AMJ Capital. More on the <a href="/teaching/">Teaching</a> page.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section label="The courses" id="courses">
    <CurriculumMap />
    <ul class="rows bk-wide">
      {courses.map((c) => (
        <li class="grid">
          <div class="label">{c.code}<br />{c.when}</div>
          <div class="body">
            <a class="title" href={`/bucknell/${c.slug}/`}>{c.title} →</a>
            <p>{arrows(c.line)}</p>
            <p class="who"><span class="label">Students</span>{students(c)}</p>
            <p class="sample"><a href={`/bucknell/${c.slug}/`}>{c.sample}</a></p>
            <p class="sample"><a href={`/bucknell/${c.slug}/pack/`}>{c.pack}</a></p>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <div class="grid"><div class="span-8">
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">What I can cover, in a sentence: 2 sections of ANOP 102 and 1 of ANOP 330 a term, and ANOP 400 when asked - about 150 students a year. The sections are the chair's call, and ANOP 302 can take a slot in either year. It's a starting point - I'll fit it to what the department needs. Codes and prerequisites are from the <a href={catalogue} target="_blank" rel="noopener">2026-27 catalogue</a>.</p>
    </div></div>
  </Section>

  <Section label="Try a class" id="try">
    <ul class="rows bk-wide">
      <li class="grid">
        <div class="label">ANOP 102<br />Week 3</div>
        <div class="body">
          <a class="title" href="/bucknell/anop-102/#pivot">Clean it before you count it →</a>
          <p>A coffee cart's sales export, a pivot table, and 3 fixes that change who's on top.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="grid">
        <div class="label">ANOP 102<br />Week 6</div>
        <div class="body">
          <a class="title" href="/bucknell/anop-102/#breakeven">How wrong can the forecast be? →</a>
          <p>A taco truck's profit for every price and every volume at once, and the breakeven that moves with the assumptions.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="grid">
        <div class="label">ANOP 102<br />Week 8</div>
        <div class="body">
          <a class="title" href="/bucknell/anop-102/#llm">An LLM gives you probabilities →</a>
          <p>How an LLM picks its next word, and how a decision model should use what it says.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="grid">
        <div class="label">ANOP 102<br />Week 11</div>
        <div class="body">
          <a class="title" href="/bucknell/anop-102/#regression">One weekend flips the slope →</a>
          <p>12 weeks of ad spend and sales, a fitted line, and the one weekend that decides whether the ads pay.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="grid">
        <div class="label">ANOP 330<br />Week 8</div>
        <div class="body">
          <a class="title" href="/bucknell/anop-330/#threshold">The most accurate cutoff earns nothing →</a>
          <p>1,000 customers, 100 about to cancel, and a retention offer. Watch accuracy and money pull in opposite directions.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="grid">
        <div class="label">ANOP 330<br />Week 4</div>
        <div class="body">
          <a class="title" href="/bucknell/anop-330/#overfit">The model that memorised the past →</a>
          <p>Fit a curve to 16 days of sales, pick the degree you'd ship, then reveal the 8 days it never saw.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="grid">
        <div class="label">ANOP 302<br />Week 12</div>
        <div class="body">
          <a class="title" href="/bucknell/anop-302/#try">Price an option by simulation →</a>
          <p>Simulate stock paths and watch the estimate close in on Black-Scholes.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Section>
</Base>
